# Line endings are normalized to LF, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, every tracked text file in this repo read as
# modified because the working tree held CRLF while every blob in HEAD is LF.
# `git status` listed 106 files with no real changes in them, which made
# `git add -A` dangerous (it would sweep ~25,000 lines of line-ending churn into
# a branch) and buried the two files that genuinely had pending edits.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain `text=auto`: everything this repo produces runs on
# Linux -- Docker images for the backend and the nginx-fronted web kiosk, the
# shell entrypoints those images execute, and GitHub Actions runners. A CRLF
# shebang line makes a shell script fail with a confusing "bad interpreter"
# error, so LF in the working tree is the safer default here even when someone
# edits on Windows. Modern Windows editors all handle LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never touched, never diffed as text. text=auto would normally
# detect these, but declaring them explicitly means a corrupt-by-normalization
# bug can't happen even if detection is wrong.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary

# Generated; keep them out of diffs and review, but still normalized as text.
package-lock.json -diff
